      "message": "There are many old libbinder SM APIs and also pingBinder which mix EX_* and status_t. Theoretically, the error codes could even conflict, though I never found a case where this was a problem in practice. I\u0027ve looked at unmixing them before (e.g. b/115654595 - looks like I didn\u0027t leave many notes...), especially when I was originally making libbinder_ndk, because it uses many \u0027prune\u0027 functions to make sure only recognized codes are returned. However, I believe CPP/Java backends are too far gone to properly unmix these codes, and changing them now may cause app compat issues. So I think baring technological progress in automated refactoring, given that they do work, the indefinite policy should be to freeze and document them.",
